            {
                "entry_id": "bf26665f-efd4-3bb1-8a8e-4157a2eab054",
                "word": "ichor",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "be44f309-79c2-4ff1-b3c4-5d5919c46fad",
                        "entry_id": "bf26665f-efd4-3bb1-8a8e-4157a2eab054",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "ichors"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "456da626-a721-39c8-981f-6b79e3190f0f",
                        "entry_id": "bf26665f-efd4-3bb1-8a8e-4157a2eab054",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Sang aqueux mêlé de pus âcre, qui est le produit d’une inflammation."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d560ee28-d08b-4c7d-a955-d8ecd57387a1",
                                "sense_id": "456da626-a721-39c8-981f-6b79e3190f0f",
                                "text": "On doit, sans perdre un instant, extirper la tumeur : opération qui exige la main d’un anatomiste, et qui n’est pas sans danger pour celui qui la pratique, l’inoculation de l’ichor gangreneux pouvant causer la mort."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "485094c8-c594-3caf-95a9-6364ebfa84a7",
                        "entry_id": "bf26665f-efd4-3bb1-8a8e-4157a2eab054",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Chez Homère, liquide qui coule dans les veines des dieux et leur sert de sang."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Mythologie grecque"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "629101fd-704c-3682-beab-6a49d2105132",
                        "entry_id": "bf26665f-efd4-3bb1-8a8e-4157a2eab054",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Substance minérale émanant du magma puis se solidifie et métamorphise certaines roches."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c99f291f-4966-406e-b762-ae64e50c7ed0",
                        "source_entry_id": "bf26665f-efd4-3bb1-8a8e-4157a2eab054",
                        "target_lang_word": "ichor",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "ichor",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3adb7fd6-46e5-3c9a-a9d9-83a6fe19d049",
                                        "entry_id": "4a562f26-a038-363a-9cc3-fba73eae2472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The liquid said to flow in place of blood in the veins of the gods."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Greek",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d955636-f50c-4966-b51e-4253b8842767",
                                                "sense_id": "3adb7fd6-46e5-3c9a-a9d9-83a6fe19d049",
                                                "text": "This ſaid, ſhe wip’d from Venus’ wounded Palm / The ſacred Ichor, and infus’d the Balm."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21d33d44-83a3-44b3-ad1c-b5054b973b33",
                                                "sense_id": "3adb7fd6-46e5-3c9a-a9d9-83a6fe19d049",
                                                "text": "With his protruded ſpear her gentle hand / He wounded, piercing through her thin attire / Ambroſial, by themſelves the Graces wrought, / Her inſide wriſt, faſt by her roſy palm. / Blood follow'd, but immortal; ichor pure, / Such as the bleſt inhabitants of heav'n / May bleed, nectareous; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a95ef3b-4000-43bc-92ff-c35330e7d721",
                                                "sense_id": "3adb7fd6-46e5-3c9a-a9d9-83a6fe19d049",
                                                "text": "He [Saint Peter] potter'd with his keys at a great rate, / And sweated through his apostolic skin: / Of course his perspiration was but ichor, / Or some such other spiritual liquor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e27e69fb-5ef4-31b4-b18a-e47254ee7fd7",
                                        "entry_id": "4a562f26-a038-363a-9cc3-fba73eae2472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The blood of human beings or animals; also (obsolete) the clear, fluid portion of blood; blood plasma, plasma."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable",
                                            "poetic",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f7cbfff-0c46-475e-adbc-6aeab67e9874",
                                                "sense_id": "e27e69fb-5ef4-31b4-b18a-e47254ee7fd7",
                                                "text": "He had merely meant to express his feeling that the streams which ran through their veins were not yet purified by time to that perfection, had not become so genuine an ichor, as to be worthy of being called blood in the genealogical sense."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7705b486-f274-3ecf-8ea4-abf3c1e9a5d6",
                                        "entry_id": "4a562f26-a038-363a-9cc3-fba73eae2472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A blood-like fluid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "poetic",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f862ef6-3b20-4e6c-ae4f-a1f073f4893d",
                                                "sense_id": "7705b486-f274-3ecf-8ea4-abf3c1e9a5d6",
                                                "text": "[I]chores and thoſe ſerious matters being thickned become flegme, and flegme degenerates into choler, choler aduſt becomes æruginoſa melancholia, as vinegar out of the pureſt wine putrified or by exhalation of purer ſpirits is ſo made, and becomes ſowre and ſharp; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "630a9cdf-9d4c-4f3c-864f-332b4d8761e7",
                                                "sense_id": "7705b486-f274-3ecf-8ea4-abf3c1e9a5d6",
                                                "text": "Go bring him [an ant] home to his people. / Lay him in state on a sepal. / Wrap him for shroud in a petal. / Embalm him with ichor of nettle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1a844fd5-b466-4c9b-a0e2-3ad8be27e33e",
                                                "sense_id": "7705b486-f274-3ecf-8ea4-abf3c1e9a5d6",
                                                "text": "They will not live / As shades but angle forward to enjoy / The pluck of life, the pressure of their ichor."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d79169b7-d912-4ba6-8a1e-f6517cb654d4",
                                                "sense_id": "7705b486-f274-3ecf-8ea4-abf3c1e9a5d6",
                                                "text": "Like snow fall you cry a silent storm. / Your tears paint rivers on this oaken wall / Amber nectar / misery ichor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6f3ae4c-09e4-36a7-ab0f-6d5125f78534",
                                        "entry_id": "4a562f26-a038-363a-9cc3-fba73eae2472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fluid believed to seep out from magma and cause rock to turn into granite."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "73fca92a-86f9-3a13-88fe-141a2bebb1a2",
                                        "entry_id": "4a562f26-a038-363a-9cc3-fba73eae2472",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fetid, watery discharge from a sore; pus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "91281f1d-d71c-4f77-a50d-203e762ea13b",
                        "source_entry_id": "bf26665f-efd4-3bb1-8a8e-4157a2eab054",
                        "target_lang_word": "icor",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "icor",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eedcafd8-abd8-38f0-8ccc-0b86dafd828c",
                                        "entry_id": "afd13e16-7df6-374d-aa56-520fa018e099",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fluido claro que cumple la función de la sangre en los dioses, obtenido de la ambrosía y el néctar que estos consumen."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ef9118c2-68a2-4a0d-8a3a-72194117f183",
                                                "sense_id": "eedcafd8-abd8-38f0-8ccc-0b86dafd828c",
                                                "text": "y derramó así el icor, la sangre inmortal que se agita en las venas de los bienaventurados dioses; pues ellos no comen del pan, ni beben del negro vino, y su sangre no es como la nuestra y son llamados inmortales."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "df9c548f-6824-4de8-bb68-d92a97de34ba",
                                                "sense_id": "eedcafd8-abd8-38f0-8ccc-0b86dafd828c",
                                                "text": "una sangre sutil y delicada y etérea, como el icor de las deidades del Olimpo."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c4d3a8b2-aa9c-3835-9dfb-39860e6332d1",
                                        "entry_id": "afd13e16-7df6-374d-aa56-520fa018e099",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Fluido similar al pus, de color claro y consistencia similar al suero, que los antiguos médicos identificaban como secreción de algunas lesiones ulcerosas de la piel."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d5c36a7-5735-4814-b6c4-cf053a590b2e",
                                                "sense_id": "c4d3a8b2-aa9c-3835-9dfb-39860e6332d1",
                                                "text": "Las afecciones crónicas dan más comunmente lugar á colecciones ó secreciones icorosas, lo que sucede en el cáncer, la gota, en el reumatismo y aun en las herpes. Este icor consiste en una serosidad inocente si está enquistada, corrosiva si es segregada en superficies libres, y aun inoculable y capaz de hacer el papel de vírus como en algunas enfermedades herpéticas y escrofulosas."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3f66408c-b63e-3be0-af16-96a9329e4ea2",
                                        "entry_id": "afd13e16-7df6-374d-aa56-520fa018e099",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Líquido amargo, de color amarillo verdoso, segregado por el hígado."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"3\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "51e66858-2322-3319-9692-e567bfaa8878",
                                        "entry_id": "afd13e16-7df6-374d-aa56-520fa018e099",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "fluido similar a la sangre que se encuentra en diversos seres sobrenaturales, demoníacos o extraterrestres."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"4\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
